(*
expect:
3
97
98
99
4
#a
#ab
#b
*)
(* rete#205 — a Symbol answers at:/size over its NAME bytes, so nothing has to
   build a String to read them.

   This is the gate for a PERFORMANCE fix, which is why it asserts SEMANTICS and
   not a number: the win (71% of the node's C-heap allocation, one of only two
   C-heap allocators there) is measured by an allocation window on hardware, but
   what could silently break is the ORDER, and order is what every Map, every
   value `=` and every encoded frame depends on.

   Two properties, deliberately together:
     1. at:/size read the name WITHOUT the '#' that printString prefixes — hence
        `#abc size` = 3 while `#abc printString size` = 4. If a future change
        routed this back through printString, `at: 1` would answer $# (35) for
        every Symbol alike and this test would say so.
     2. Symbol ordering is IDENTICAL to what comparing printStrings gave, which
        is what a Map's canonical key order is built on. Both operands in the
        rank-6 arm are Symbols, so the shared '#' cancelled — and #a/#ab is the
        exact-prefix tie, the case where an off-by-one in the old '#'-skipping
        would have hidden. *)
class SymbolBytes packageUsing: manifest = () (
public main: platform args: args = (
  | M m |
  #abc size printString out.
  (#abc at: 1) printString out.
  (#abc at: 2) printString out.
  (#abc at: 3) printString out.
  #abc printString size printString out.

  M:: platform Map.
  m:: M with: #b -> 1 with: #ab -> 2 with: #a -> 3.
  m keysDo: [ :k | k printString out ].
)
) : (
)
